# FLOOWBOX - Client Onboarding Email Sequence

Every new client at FLOOWBOX used to get the same manually written emails — welcome, checklist, follow-up. This workflow automates the entire sequence while keeping each email personalized.

## What it does

When a new client signs up, a webhook triggers a 3-email sequence over 4 days. The Day 0 welcome email is written by GPT-4o in real-time using the client's name, company, and specific service — so it never feels templated. Day 1 sends a requirements checklist. Day 4 sends a gentle check-in if the client hasn't responded.

## Tools Used
- **Orchestration:** n8n
- **AI:** OpenAI GPT-4o (personalized welcome email generation)
- **Email:** SMTP / Gmail
- **Timing:** n8n Wait nodes (1 day + 3 day delays)
- **Trigger:** Webhook (connect to your signup form or CRM)

## Email Sequence

```
Day 0 → Personalized welcome (GPT-4o written, 200 words)
Day 1 → Requirements checklist (what we need to start)
Day 4 → Check-in (if no reply yet)
```

## Why I built this

When FLOOWBOX had 3-4 active clients, I was writing the same emails manually every time someone signed up. The welcome email especially — I wanted it to feel personal every time. GPT-4o generates a fresh one using the client's actual context, so it reads like I wrote it specifically for them.

## What GPT-4o personalizes

The welcome email includes:
- Client's name and company
- Specific service they signed up for
- Tone adapted to the service type (technical vs business)
- Natural sign-off as Navtej

## Setup

1. Connect your signup form / CRM to send POST to webhook
2. Add SMTP credentials (Gmail / custom domain)
3. Add OpenAI API key
4. Customize the prompt with your own company and founder name

## Extending this

Add a Day 7 "project kickoff" email once the discovery call is done. Or connect to Calendly webhook to automatically send the checklist after a call is booked.
